.Dd $Mdocdate: August 2 2026 $
.Dt Fugu::SSH 3p
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm Fugu::SSH
.Nd run a command on another machine over SSH
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Bd -literal
use Fugu::SSH;

my $ssh = Fugu::SSH->new(
    host => '127.0.0.1',
    port => 2222,
    user => 'root',
);

$ssh->wait_available(120) or die "the host never answered\en";

my $result = $ssh->run_command('uname -a');
print $result->{stdout};
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
wraps
.Xr Net::SSH2 3p
for the two things a provisioning tool does: run a command and capture
its output, and write a file.
An interactive session falls back to
.Xr ssh 1 ,
because
.Xr Net::SSH2 3p
does not give correct control of a terminal.
.Pp
.Xr Net::SSH2 3p
loads at connect time and not at compile time.
Thus the module keeps the core-Perl load contract of Fugu, and an
installation without the library still loads it and fails with a clear
message at the first connect.
.Pp
Authentication tries the SSH agent first, when
.Ev SSH_AUTH_SOCK
is set, and falls back to the password when the caller gave one.
.Ss new
.Fn new "%args"
creates a connection object.
The method opens nothing: every other method connects for itself and
disconnects when it is done.
.Pp
These are the arguments:
.Bl -tag -width "passwordXX"
.It Fa host
The host to reach.
The default is
.Ql 127.0.0.1 .
.It Fa port
The port.
The default is 22.
.It Fa user
The user to log in as.
The default is
.Ql root .
.It Fa password
The password, for a host that has no key yet.
.It Fa timeout
The connection timeout in seconds.
The default is 10.
.El
.Ss run_command
.Fn run_command "$command"
runs one command and returns a hash reference with
.Va stdout ,
.Va stderr
and
.Va exit_code .
A connection that fails reports exit code 1 and a message in
.Va stderr .
.Ss write_file
.Fn write_file "$remote_path" "$content" "$mode"
writes a file over SFTP.
The default mode is 0644.
.Pp
The method checks the length that the write reported.
A provisioning script that arrives half-written is worse than one that
never arrived.
.Ss is_available
.Fn is_available
reports if the host takes an authenticated connection now.
.Ss wait_available
.Fn wait_available "$timeout"
polls until the host takes a connection, or until the timeout ends.
The default timeout is 120 seconds.
.Pp
The wait stops early when a signal arrives, through
.Xr Fugu::Timeout 3p .
A poll loop must not outlive the interrupt that told the program to
stop.
.Ss interactive
.Fn interactive
runs
.Xr ssh 1
with the terminal of the caller and returns its exit code.
.Pp
The code is a value between 0 and 255, and not a raw wait status.
A caller that passed the raw status to
.Ic exit
would turn a remote exit code of 1 into
.Ql exit(256) ,
which the kernel truncates to 0, and a failed remote command would
read as a success.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn run_command
returns a hash reference.
.Pp
.Fn write_file
returns 0 on success and 1 on failure, like a command.
.Pp
.Fn is_available
and
.Fn wait_available
return 1 or 0.
.Fn interactive
returns an exit code.
.Sh ERRORS
Every method dies when
.Xr Net::SSH2 3p
is not installed.
The message names the module, because that failure is an installation
problem and not a connection problem.
.Pp
No method dies for a connection that fails.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ssh 1 ,
.Xr Fugu::Process 3p ,
.Xr Fugu::Timeout 3p ,
.Xr Net::SSH2 3p
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Dick Olsson Aq Mt hi@senzilla.io
.Sh CAVEATS
Every method opens its own connection and closes it at the end.
A caller that runs many commands pays the handshake for each one.
.Pp
.Fn run_command
holds the whole output of the command in memory.
.Pp
The module does not verify the host key.
It is a provisioning tool for a machine that the caller just created,
on a port on the loopback address.
Do not use it to reach a host across a network you do not trust.
